        "message": "Here are three practical things you can try right now: 1. **Write it down:** Keep a notepad nearby and do a quick brain dump of everything on your mind for tomorrow. Jotting down even a single, concrete first step for each task lets your brain set them aside until morning.\n2. **The 20-minute reset:** If you have been lying awake worrying for more than 15 or 20 minutes, get out of bed. Move to a dimly lit room and do something low-key—like reading a book or listening to quiet audio—until you feel sleepy, then go back to bed. This keeps your bed from feeling like a place to worry.\n3. **Give your mind a low-stakes task:** If your thoughts keep racing, switch your attention to something neutral. Try mentally naming an animal or city for each letter of the alphabet, or focus purely on the physical sensation of breathing out slowly. Pick whichever one feels easiest to do right now and see how it works for you.",
